The '''2026–27 Thai League 1''' will be the 10th season of [[Thai League 1]] under its current name and the 30th season of top-flight Thai [[Association football|football]] professional league since its establishment in 1996. This league is also known as '''BYD Sealion 6 League I''' due to the sponsorship deal with [[BYD Auto]]. The season is scheduled to begin on 4 September 2026 and will conclude on 30 May 2027. 

[[Buriram United F.C.|Buriram United]] entered the season as the [[List of Thai football champions|five-time defending champions]], having won their fifth consecutive league title and 12th overall Thai top-flight football title the previous season.<ref>{{cite web |title=Buriram blitz seals 10th title |work=Bangkok Post |url=https://www.bangkokpost.com/sports/3015791/buriram-blitz-seals-10th-title |last1=Chittinand |first1=Tor |date=2 May 2025 }}</ref>

In this season, there is a change in the Thai League 1’s foreign player rules, as the ASEAN Quota is abolished.<ref>{{cite web |title=Fandi brothers could be affected by changes to Thai League 1's foreign player rules |url=https://www.straitstimes.com/sport/football/fandi-brothers-could-be-affected-by-changes-to-thai-league-1s-foreign-player-rules}}</ref>

== Overview ==
=== Promotion and relegation (pre-season) ===
16 teams will compete in the league – the thirteen teams from previous season and three teams promoted from [[2025–26 Thai League 2|Thai League 2]].

==== Teams promoted from Thai League 2 ====
[[Rasisalai United F.C.|Rasisalai United]] and [[Sisaket United F.C.|Sisaket United]] became the first two teams to be promoted on 18 April 2026 & 25 April 2026 after winning their respective matches. [[Pattani F.C.|Pattani]] became the last team to be promoted after their win on penalties against [[Nongbua Pitchaya F.C.|Nongbua Pitchaya]]. It was 3–3 on aggregate in the promotion play-off.<ref>{{cite web |title=Pattani seal historic T1 promotion  Please credit and share this article with others using this link: https://www.bangkokpost.com/sports/3260208/pattani-seal-historic-t1-promotion. View our policies at http://goo.gl/9HgTd and http://goo.gl/ou6Ip. © Bangkok Post PCL. All rights reserved. |url=https://www.bangkokpost.com/sports/3260208/pattani-seal-historic-t1-promotion}}</ref>

Rasisalai & Pattani United secured back-to-back promotion and where promoted to the top tier for the first time in their histories while Sisaket United also secured promotion to the top tier for the first time in their history, thus all the 3 teams promoted are competing in top tier for the first time in their histories.

